-- The heading-line spelling of a section binder, `§ NAME GIVEN …`, falls under
-- the same column rule (the GIVEN keyword sits at a column greater than the §)
-- and the parser accepts it. It is NOT the house style: prettyLayout re-emits
-- the indented form, and this file's .ep.golden is the witness that exact
-- printing keeps whichever form was written.

§ `S` GIVEN a IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`a plus one` MEANS a PLUS 1

#CHECK `a plus one`
